Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-14-2000||09:08 PM||||<BR>Hey guys, hope the weekend is going or went well.<P>Was out-of-town this weekend for mother's day and happened up on a Formula and want your thoughts.<P>Of course it is an '88, but this one is automatic, yellow, approx 126k miles, bare bones formula.  No t-tops, no cruise, no rear defrost, no power windows, no power mirrors, and no stereo.  The guy on the phone (btw not the owner) said it has been sitting for a while.<P>Besides being bare boned, the thing is faded and is missing the left front headlight, has a broken left front fender, and the front facia is messed up (not bent, possibly repairable). <P>The seats were covered with seat covers (probably hidding other major flaws) the interior is in other disrepair, the tires are bald, and it will need a major tune up (plugs, wires, fuel filter, fuel pump, distributer cap and rotor - minimum to get it running - if it runs at all).<P>I dont know if there is frame damage, or other hidden damage, but I'm thinking it is worth about $200.00 as it sits, based on the condition that I saw from a 3 minute perusal of the Fiero. BTW, I grabbed the VIN if that makes any difference.<P>Is it worth my investment, opinions please?<BR>||||reg||5
