Z||000007||Gold-86SE||05-16-2000||03:19 PM||||<BR>UPDATE<P>Here is what I found out today.<P>The Fiero has been at this shop for about two months.  Based on what the owner said, sounds like the driver hit a deer while in the country and took it to the closest automotive shop. A deer would explain the damage, I mentioned above, to the front end.<P>Also the mechanic/owner believes that the head is cracked. Now what that means is beyond me, because this guys knows squat about the Fiero, he admitted such - at least he is smart enough to do that.<P>If the head is cracked, what will I need to do to fix it. Please help me with a best case / worse case scenario and guesstimated costs, thanks.<P>Additionally, the owners do not live in the town where the car is located, I don't know if that is in my favor or not.<P>Assuming the owners want to sell, at most what would you guys pay for this Fiero, keep in mind the previous mentioned equipment and damage?<BR>||||reg||1
